  "findings": [
    "Native link owner now defines both real USB integration hooks; maps owned DP/PHY/clock/GPIO ranges, verifies shared supplies, reads physical CC orientation, retrains after HPD/link loss, and retains ownership across failed stop.",
    "HBR3 MX vote uses cmd-db ARC level indices and actual RSC status/completion. Busy TCS is never overwritten; timed-out active commands are retained and later reaped, not aborted.",
    "Permanent IRQ115 shared handler acknowledges only owned INTF0 bits24/25. Atomic publication, in-flight drain, bounded stop/retry and else-thread_block race handling are production-tested. No timer synthesizes VSync.",
    "Presentation validates two disjoint qualified buffers before memory writes, copies/cleans before CTL flush, completes only after a real frame/flush latch, and preserves DMA/tag ownership on teardown timeout. 10000 alternating flips pass ASanUBSan.",
    "External IOMFB adapter uses the exact original 483-slot class ABI, real EDID IOAV timing, original 53-line notification/completion bodies, GPU producer-fence gating and generation tags. Cancelled/late callbacks cannot retire a later request. This adapter is not yet connected to a qualified native DMA allocation.",
    "Actual selected DisplayDxe GOP single-display size path272c..2740 computes visible width*height*bytesPerPixel; publish2994..29a8 does not advertise unused reserved tail. No independent Display DMA mapping can be inferred from the reservation."
  ],
